# Lightweight Delivery Lane (cite)

Authoritative behavior: `docs/behavior/lightweight-delivery-lane.md`.
Skill: `.cursor/skills/lightweight-delivery-lane/SKILL.md`.
Pipeline wiring: `.cursor/skills/delivery-pipeline/SKILL.md`.

## Confirmed

- `delivery_lane: light` may skip stages **5–7** and **10** **only** when BDD proves no
  user-facing management-UI acceptance **and** no runtime/OpenAPI/Flyway/generation
  acceptance surface (docs/governance/scaffold or proven N/A unit-only leaves).
- `delivery_lane: full` remains **default** for product behavior work. Doubt → **full**.
- Light lane **must not** weaken full leaves, waive worktree, or skip unit/verify gates
  when code is touched.
- Worktree isolation remains mandatory for multi-file delivery unless user `main-only` /
  `no-worktree`. Light ≠ main-only.
